214. /// Implementers must guarantee that:
215. ///
216. /// - `as_mut_ptr()` returns a stable pointer to a backing region of at least `STORAGE_SIZE`
217. ///   bytes for the allocator lifetime.
218. /// - the backing region is writable and properly aligned for any allocation site that uses this
219. ///   backend.
220. /// - the backing region is exclusively managed by this allocator API, so creating `&'static mut`
221. ///   references from slots cannot alias with other mutable references.
